@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;design;motion] library-one-foot-bar
Library destinations MUST register their bar through FootPill or FootFree. One
FootBarLayer in the shell draws the active registration over the pages. A page change
MUST keep that layer in place; the contents change through Pully's blur fade and the
pill's width eases to its new size. Disposed registrations MUST stop owning the bar.
Source: pulls.review kit-one-foot-bar, DESIGN rule 196, FootBar.kt at
ee5cf358333cb1170f1923c7118e12af3f265b74; requested by Tavi on 22 October 2026.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] library-bars-rest-alike
Every library foot bar MUST use floatingBar for its position: 12dp in from the sides,
16dp above the system navigation bar, and raised by the keyboard. Screens MUST NOT
add their own bottom offset to the bar. The bar floats over the content without a
solid strip behind it and carries Pully's two-layer downward canvas shadow. The
navigation capsule and the Search circle are 56dp tall, with an 8dp highlight inset.
Source: pulls.review kit-bottom-bars-rest-alike, DESIGN rules 192 and 45, Kit.kt at
ee5cf358333cb1170f1923c7118e12af3f265b74; geometry from Tavi's Google Photos
comparison in the recorded review of 22 October 2026 ("less tall", "start a bit
further to the left", "a bit wider").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] library-foot-bar-owns-its-taps
A tap anywhere inside the search pill, including its edge and padding, MUST focus
its field or expand its compact form. A tap on the navigation capsule's padding
MUST NOT open a card underneath it. Search and navigation controls MUST have touch
targets of at least 44dp.
Source: pulls.review kit-foot-bar-owns-its-taps, DESIGN rule 198, FootBar.kt at
ee5cf358333cb1170f1923c7118e12af3f265b74.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] library-navigation-is-the-gallery-capsule
The library navigation capsule MUST offer Everything and Spaces, with Search as a
separate circular control showing a magnifier with a sparkle. It MUST NOT add a Create
tab. As in Google Photos, the selected highlight MUST hug the selected tab's icon and
label rather than fill half the capsule, while each tab keeps half the capsule as its
touch target; the first tab sits at the start and the last at the end. The highlight
MUST slide and resize between tabs on Pully's capsule curve; when system animations
are disabled it MUST finish immediately. Changing the selected tab MUST preserve the
one bar registration rather than creating a second visible bar. Labels are medium
weight, the unselected one in a dark grey. Only the selected tab MAY show its filled
icon; both tab labels MUST remain visible. Narrow widths and large system text MAY
hide the selected icon to preserve label space and touch targets.
Source: Tavi's Google Photos reference and no-Create decision, 22 October 2026; the
recorded review of 23 October 2026 ("some of our buttons, they're like off somehow",
"the Google font ... has a higher weight", "look at their icon inside");
pulls.review kit-segment-highlight-slides, DESIGN rule 67, Kit.kt at
ee5cf358333cb1170f1923c7118e12af3f265b74.
